        <mxCell id="rules" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#333333;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;KEY RULES (Stage 2 — Kear call confirmed)&lt;/b&gt;  1. Step 0 fires FIRST — before CONTRACT_ID lookup.  2. EVERY Kafka event (PF, NPF, NRPT, Replay) creates a NEW ROW in BOTH RDH_TRADE_LINEAGE and RDH_PERSISTENCE — Kear confirmed.  3. NPF: new row in both tables, same MIFID_LINK_ID + TRN carried forward.  4. Replay: new row in both tables, REPLAY_FLAG=Y, same MIFID_LINK_ID.  5. PF/NRPT: new MIFID_LINK_ID, new TRN, new Persistence row.  6. ROOT_LINK_ID = first event MIFID_LINK_ID — new column for full audit trail.  7. MIFID_ACTION = NULL after Stage 2. Stage 3 sets NEWT/REPL/CANC.  8. IS_NRPT=Y: set once, never reverts, propagates to all children.  ⚠ One vs multiple linkage tables (regime-specific): open action on Kear (A1)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="860" x="250" y="1250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
