        <mxCell id="vOGihw5DsFz4zbwunT8B-41" parent="vOGihw5DsFz4zbwunT8B-2" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF8E1;fontColor=#B45309;strokeColor=#B45309;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;⚠ Open points from Kear + team call (18 Jun 2026):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;(1) FAIL handling: suppress within RDP, or send to Trax for rejection? Team discussed but no firm decision — leaned toward suppressing in RDP.&lt;br/&gt;(2) CANC arriving on top of a FAIL (where original was NEWT/REPL): team agreed the CANC should be allowed through — do not fail it. Confirm and implement separately.&lt;br/&gt;(3) Trax NACK/feedback handling: whether a SENT record should be overridden if Trax returns a NACK — out of scope for now (&quot;get the basic bit done first&quot; — Kear).&lt;br/&gt;(4) Should new version stay in FAIL, or publish as-is when previous was in FAIL? Still not resolved by Kear." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="2000" x="10" y="1160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
